<title>MEXICO: GMD says to build Colombia hydro project.</title>
<headline>GMD says to build Colombia hydro project.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican construction company Grupo Mexicano de Desarrollo (GMD) said on Thursday that it will take part in the consortium building the Miel 1 hydroelectric project in Colombia.</p>
<p>In a statement the company said the project would involve damming the Miel River by constructing a concrete wall 180 meters high.</p>
<p>The hydro-electric project will have an installed capacity of 374 megwatts.</p>
<p>-- Mexico City newsroom +525 728 9559))</p>
